tb470 IE520 stack · 2026-09-03 · RESULT: port-configurable; OPERATIONAL PROOF DEFERRED (link swap)

The port accepts `speed 100`, but only on a 1G SFP port with a 10/100/1000 copper SFP:
  - empty 1G port (port2.0.2): speed 100  ACCEPTED   (port-level capability)
  - AT-SPTXc  (1000BASE-T, port2.0.9):    speed 100  ACCEPTED
  - AT-SP10TM (10GBASE-T, port2.0.1):     speed 100  REJECTED (10G-T module -> 1000-only in a 1G port)
Operational verification (link up at 100 -> MAC/Phy TLV: MAU 100BaseTXFD) needs the AT-SPTXc
cabled to a 100-capable partner. DEFERRED — link swap to be done later (Terrence, 2026-09-03).
